    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on 2026-08-12, **Corbin Carroll** is our undeniable anchor, boasting a dominant 87.14 score against Feltner. The combination of an elite matchup against a high-xERA arm and the benefit of hitting second provides a massive ceiling for both runs and stolen bases. Close behind are **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **Gabriel Moreno** (71.10); **Mickey Moniak** is effectively utilizing a significant +14% platoon edge against Kelly, while **Gabriel Moreno** benefits from the same favorable matchup against Feltner. **Isaac Paredes** (70.97) also grades out as a primary engine today, with his +9% platoon advantage and prime spot in the order driving his high efficiency. \n\nWe are monitoring the lineup for **Seiya Suzuki**, whose projected 63.11 assumes the #2 spot; should he drop down the order, his efficiency will shift, though his park and platoon metrics remain favorable against Kent. The most difficult decision at the bottom of the order was bypassing **Henry Bolte** (41.35) in favor of **Zach McKinstry** (47.30). While **Henry Bolte** benefits from a strong park factor against Rasmussen, **Zach McKinstry** is slated for a high-leverage speed opportunity against a slower pitcher delivery; his \"slow SP delivery\" tag provides a rare marginal gain for our stolen base-starved 5x5 build. We are holding tight on **Austin Riley** (59.34), who is effectively our utility floor today, as we navigate the continued absences of **James Wood**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** on the IL. With **Cole Young** and **Max Muncy** facing a tougher test against Rasmussen, our focus remains on maximizing the sprint speed potential of our outfield trio to maintain our competitive edge in the SB category.",
